he docs-authoring priority exception, not from HLR-4's P2 label. |\n63\t\n64\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n65\t\n66\t## Component Classification\n67\t\n68\t| Component | Classification | Rationale |\n69\t|-----------|----------------|-----------|\n70\t| Dashboard | Active | Comparison view (E001) and registry entry point (E003) are Dashboard code changes. |\n71\t| Model Registry | Active | Producing-run link on model versions (E002) is a Model Registry change. |\n72\t| Data Science Pipelines | Passive | No code change stated; pipeline runs are already surfaced to the Dashboard via the KFP v2 API (per architecture context). Validation that comparisons render correctly for pipeline runs is an acceptance criterion on E001. |\n73\t\n74\tComponent names are copied verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`\n75\t(Dashboard, Model Registry, Data Science Pipelines, Documentation). The\n76\tdocumentation epic uses the canonical `Documentation` component; no\n77\tnon-obvious mappings were needed.\n78\t\n79\t## Health Warnings\n80\t\n81\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n82\t   Teams table, no per-component change/owner detail (Affected Components is a\n83\t   bare list), no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n84\t   and no non-functional requirements. Owning teams were assigned from the\n85\t   architecture-context files (`dashboard.md`, `model-registry.md`,\n86\t   `data-science-pipelines.md`). If actual team ownership differs, E002/E003\n87\t   team assignments should be corrected at planning time.\n88\t2. **Data Science Pipelines assumed passive**: the strategy lists it as\n89\t   affected but describes no change. If comparison requires Data Science\n90\t   Pipelines-side changes (e.g. exposing run parameters/metrics in a new form),\n91\t   a separate epic owned by the RHOAI Pipelines team must be added.\n92\t3. **No priority inversions detected**: P0 (comparison view) is a root epi