{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b463084fe1fcc0d0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Link registered model versions to producing runs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Link registered model versions to producing runs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRecord, on each registered model version in the Model Registry, a link back to\n34\tthe training or pipeline run that produced it, using the registry's existing\n35\tmetadata extension point on model versions. This makes the producing run\n36\tprogrammatically resolvable so a run comparison can later be opened from the\n37\tModel Registry.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Model version metadata carries a reference to the run that produced it (run\n42\t  type and run identifier), via the Model Registry's custom-properties\n43\t  extension point on ModelVersion entities.\n44\t- The link is settable and readable through the Model Registry REST API so\n45\t  that registration tooling can record it and consumers can resolve the\n46\t  originating run of any model version.\n47\t- Applies uniformly to runs from training jobs and from Data Science\n48\t  Pipelines.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A registered model version can carry a reference to the run that produced\n53\t  it, set and read through the Model Registry REST API (custom-properties\n54\t  extension point on ModelVersion).\n55\t- The reference distinguishes run type (training run vs pipeline run) and\n56\t  identifies the run sufficiently for a consumer to retrieve its parameters\n57\t  and metrics.\n58\t- Model versions without a producing-run link remain fully functional (the\n59\t  link is optional metadata).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-2 (P1, registry side): registered model versions link back to the run\n64\t  that produced them.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9381891f2a764639","agent_id":"a72b9122ee5648073","session_id":"e5b4410a-af76-4919-bbd4-4d16b5058733","uuid":"5b4fb1b8-7978-4a7d-9b75-7bbee67c452c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:02:44.397Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b463084fe1fcc0d0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
