licitly reuses the runs-list\n68\tselection behavior. No work-product type mixing — documentation authoring is\n69\tisolated in E004 per the work-product boundary rule. No epic exceeds the\n70\t~2-week guideline; E001 (multi-select, side-by-side, diff over one surface) is\n71\ta single-sprint-shaped change on one surface. All component names are verbatim\n72\tfrom `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\n73\t\n74\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n75\tAll four epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact\n76\t(comparison view, run-link metadata with REST API surface, registry entry\n77\tpoint, published documentation). No Investigation epics exist, which is\n78\tcorrect: the strategy lists \"Open Questions: None\" and no uncertainty changes\n79\tdownstream structure. E004 correctly carries `implementation_type:\n80\tdocs-authoring`. All `gated_by` fields are null and no epic lists an\n81\tInvestigation in `dependencies`, so no gating metadata is required; nothing is\n82\tmisclassified.\n83\t\n84\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n85\tAll epics are Implementation type and carry the 9-signal `ai_signals` set\n86\t(`investigation_signals` null) — the type-appropriate rubric. Signal values\n87\tare consistent with the rubric conditions and the strategy content:\n88\tchange_specificity 0 for functional-level scope (behavior stated concretely,\n89\tno file paths — correctly neutral rather than unfavorable), pattern_precedent\n90\tand existing_foundation +1 grounded in existing runs pages, ModelVersion\n91\tcustom properties, and the in-Dashboard registry UI, open_questions +1\n92\tmatching the strategy's empty open-questions list, and repo_access +1 for the\n93\tpublic midstream repos. E004's divergent values are correct:\n94\thuman_process_gates -1 (Red Hat docs peer/technical review gates plus the\n95\tRule 24 review AC), repo_access 0 (doc source location genuinely unconfirmed\n96\t— a defensible neutral), and architecture_claims 0 with the valid rationale\n97\tthat no architecture-context file covers the Documentation component (the\n98\trhoai-3.0 context set contains only dashboard, model-registry, and\n99\tdata-science-pipelines files). Calibration cross-check against `.context`:\n100\tE001's citation of dashboard.md, E002's and E003's citations of\n101\tmodel-registry.md, and the passive treatment of Data Science Pipelines\n102\t(KFP v2 API surfacing pipeline runs in the Dashboard) all corroborate. Signal\n103\trationales in the ai-signals files match the frontmatter values. Computed\n104\tscore/classification fields were not re-derived, per the pipeline-computed\n105\trule.\n106\t\n107\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n108\tEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria derived from the strategy. E004\n109\tcarries the Rule 24 \"technically reviewed against implementation\" AC. No\n110\treplacement of an existing platform capability occurs (the comparison view\n111\treplaces a manual spreadsheet workflow, not platform code), so Rule 23\n112\trollback/feature-flag ACs are not required; no konflux chain exists, so Rule\n113\t25 is not applicable. Scanned all ACs for externally-controlled preconditions:\n114\tnone found — the Data Science Pipelines validation AC on E001 conditions what\n115\tthe epic itself verifies, not access granted by others. Out-of-scope\n116\tboundaries (no auto-promotion, no cross-cluster/project comparison) are\n117\tencoded as negative ACs on E001 and E004. No epic body references sibling\n118\tepics by draft ID.\n119\t\n120\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n121\tThe combined epic set accounts for all strategy scope: run selection and\n122\tside-by-side view (E001), diff presentation (E001), registry lineage link for\n123\tboth training and pipeline runs (E002), registry entry point with graceful\n124\tno-link handling and run-adding (E003), and documentation covering both entry\n125\tpaths plus boundaries (E004). The out-of-scope list is respected and encoded\n126\tas ACs. Cross-epic co